{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792440000000-review-7a-custody-on-rows.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 18:30 +07\n# Review (mutation method): slice 7a, custody on rows and the rows inspector\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a`, branch `srvm-phase7a`, commit b4d80e8d (`git diff 23a8caef..HEAD`). Spec: the Architect's plan `collab/phase7-plan.md` (sections 3.1 custody on rows, 3.3 the inspector, 3.4 pack vs root id, 4 slice 7a), continuation design 2.5/2.6/5.5/7.1/7.2, transport tuples 5.5, UCF 7.2, 7.7, 7.11. Engineer report (opus; you are the non-author reviewer): `collab/1792420000000-engineer-7a-custody-on-rows.report.md` (deviations 1-8, design defects D1-D4). Owner answers: fork custody slot is `nil`; REPL custody gap accepted; install checks in 7b. Owner rulings: A only code identity; no compat shims or version dispatch; root id depends only on structure; lease/epoch/holder never enter a body; BLAKE3. Landing decision (orchestrator): 7a-7d land on an integration branch `srvm-phase7` and reach master only when 7d is green, so the 141 old-codec deftests failing in six suites (D1) are expected until 7b/7c re-base them. Check: (1) custody grammar and `custody-baseline` against plan 3.1: slot by kind, the five keys only, policy/occurrence/arbitration/next-op-seq/origin, op-seq exhaustion, fork nil, halted exclusive lowers ended, fork under :exclusive refused; each lower refusal BEFORE any attach with attach counts; the stage runs once over the whole tree after the three per-tree stages; (2) `grant` checks (seven) ported faithfully from the old inspector: diff against the version-1 `checkpoint.cljc` and the old grant code, list any check dropped or weakened; protection both directions; exact counter restore; `:fenced` minimal mode (what 7b must finish); (3) `rows.checkpoint/inspect`: address vs canonical bytes vs pack, `:yin.k/root` in the baseline (D2: opus's finding that a re-emitted variant with a different root is a `:variant-conflict`; is that the right call or must a variant with the same baseline-but-other-root be accepted? give a recommendation), decode accepting unsorted packs (D2 second point: should `rows/decode` refuse unsorted packs?); (4) `emit` sorting: one root one pack on JVM/Node/Dart (numeric/byte order of ids, comparator portability: strings vs bytes, locale); (5) fixtures: the 55 pins and 50 mutations are real (each mutation refused at the path it names, none vacuous), the anchors' full bytes reproduce, ledger-v2 digest; the harness changed one assertion (deviation 2): accept; (6) D3 doc amendments list: complete and correct; (7) portability for Node/Dart of the new code (`for`, private vars, numeric ranges incl. `max-exact`, Float64 `version-float` fixture, catches, EDN reading); (8) own mutants (cp backup; diff and git diff --quiet to verify): custody header by kind swapped; a grant check weakened to `true`; protection one direction dropped; counter restore off by one; fork under :exclusive accepted; custody stage after attach; unsorted emit; inspector skipping the root check; baseline excluding the pack address; `max-exact` off by one; the fenced mode skipping the exporting gate. Say which survive. Run `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.ucf.ledger-fixture-test -n yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant-test -n yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test` and `-i :slow`, foreground. Findings `collab/1792440000000-review-7a-custody-on-rows.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` ending VERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch) or CHANGES_REQUESTED, findings table with severity and file:line. Edit nothing else.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
